WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.060
Yes?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.730
A letter arrived for you, Monsieur Noé.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.520
For me?

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.110
It was left at the front desk.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.920
I'm waiting for you
with Mademoiselle Domi!

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.250
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.180
Let me introduce you, Noé.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.850
These are my darling grandchildren,

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.350
Louis and his little sister, Dominique.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.810
N-Nice to meet you.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.670
Dominique, I have a favor to ask.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:37.300
I want you to give this
to Noé when the time comes.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.170
Louis?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.640
You really are

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.010
just like me.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.100
Domi?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.060
Noé!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.020
What's wrong?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.230
Mina is...

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.980
Mina is to be executed tomorrow?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.280
But why?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.570
Why? Because she's a curse-bearer.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.450
A curse-bearer?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:09.410
They are beheaded by a bourreau.
That's the custom.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:13.880
Noé, I want to save Mina, too.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.250
Might we not help her flee the village?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.550
Mina.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.230
Domi, Noé.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:39.940
Blood. I want blood.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.530
Blood! Give me blood!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.820
Domi, run.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.080
Noé?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.240
Louis, snap out of it!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.370
What's the matter?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:56.090
Kill me. I want you to kill me.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.670
If I'm doomed to die, Noé...

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:03.720
If I'm doomed to die, I want you to...

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.510
...kill me!

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.930
I can't... Louis.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:29.620
Louis said he wanted you to
have this when the time came.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.540
He told me to keep it till then.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.380
Wooden stakes?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.550
Noé!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.560
Forgive me, Noé.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.490
What shall I do?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:09.700
Grandfather says it is likely
a psychological condition.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.620
Whatever shall I do?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.290
He hasn't opened his eyes for two days.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.380
What am I to do if he
never opens them again?

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.550
What am I to do?!

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.130
If only...

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.970
If only I hadn't gone to see Noé that day.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.090
If I had handled it myself...

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.510
If only I had let go of Mina,

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.060
perhaps that terrible slaughter
would have never occurred.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.320
At the very least, Noé wouldn't have
seen Louis beheaded right before his eyes.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.360
Domi?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.280
Veronica?!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:52.370
I came all this way to fetch you
after you never came home.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.160
This place is as dirty and dusty as ever.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.580
Now, get ready to leave.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.380
N-No!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.470
He ended up like this because of me.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:10.010
I cannot simply abandon him.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.220
Your little brother... Louis is dead.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.980
Don't you feel anything, dear sister?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:21.020
First of all, I do not
<i>have</i> a little brother.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.990
Moreover, he should have
been slain the day he was born.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.410
You should be thankful he
was allowed to live this long.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:38.250
Whatever are you talking about?

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.830
What?! Surely you jest, Domi!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:44.710
Are you telling me you did not know?!

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:49.130
Did you truly believe he was hidden
from the world because he was ill?

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.510
No! You are sorely mistaken!

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.890
You truly are a fool!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.100
He was hidden away because

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.100
he was your twin!

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.690
What?

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.270
My twin?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.030
Surely even you must know?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.860
Twins? Louis and I?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.330
Twins are said to rob the womb
of far more life than one child.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.330
In the vampire world,
they are a symbol of misfortune.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.120
I thought Louis was a year older than me.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.250
Should anyone learn
your mother bore twins,

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.050
it would tarnish the
good name of House de Sade.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:30.840
That's why they chose but one of you.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.890
In truth, one of you should
have been slain at birth.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:40.520
But out of the blue, Grandfather said,
"That would be a waste. I shall take him."

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.020
That's when he took Louis away.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:47.360
Even Father cannot defy Grandfather.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.030
He did say that there was
something he wished to try.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.320
Why?

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.160
Why did they choose me?

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.040
I wonder.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:04.670
Knowing Father, I imagine he decided
based on how he felt at the time.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:12.840
Then again, I have no time to waste
thinking of a little brother I never had.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.640
But if he <i>had</i> been chosen over you,

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:21.810
I wonder if he would have lived up to
our expectations more than you have.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.360
Louis.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.610
Did he know about this?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.820
Louis.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:38.030
I wish I could live here all the time.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.580
I envy you, Louis.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:50.090
How could I have said
something so awful to him?

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.840
Noe, are you all right?!
Do you know who I am?!

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.350
Noé!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.390
Noé!

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.850
Louis!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.230
Thank goodness.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.770
I dreamt that you had died.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:13.860
Thank goodness, Louis.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.740
It really was just a dream.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.460
Noé.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.380
Noe, do you, too,
wish Louis had been chosen?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.180
Do you wish that

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.350
Louis lived instead of me?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.910
You poor thing.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.700
How about calling off the search?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.950
I'll keep looking a bit longer.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:08.120
Why are you so concerned
about the Hellfire Witch?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:13.130
Isn't it in your best interest for
those two to become an item?

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:16.970
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.850
I'm sorry. Are you all right?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:27.770
Well, if you'll excuse me,
Mademoiselle Dominique.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.440
Oh, so your name is Dominique.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.940
Mikhail!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:40.780
That's my name!

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:45.200
Huh? Are you crying, mademoiselle?

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.580
You poor thing.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.290
Huh?

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:52.960
I pity you, mademoiselle.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:05.970
I wish it was I who became a curse-bearer.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.390
I wish it was I who was beheaded.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.860
I wish it was Louis

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.520
who was now by Noé's side.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:21.820
Why was it not me?

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.830
I should have died.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:29.370
If I had died...

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:33.420
Please forgive me, Noé.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.250
There, there.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:39.340
There, there. Don't cry, mademoiselle.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:43.890
I'm sure your prince will
come for you before long.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:48.430
Then the tragic princess
will find happiness,

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.310
and we can return to
our families once more.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.020
Isn't that right, mademoiselle?

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.610
Vanitas! I finally found you!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.530
Amelia?

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.030
It's Monsieur Noé!
Something terrible has happened!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.590
I bid you welcome!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:27.470
Thank you for coming, Monsieur Noé!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.180
--I am--

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.720
--Where is Domi?!
--I am--

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.310
Oh my!

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:38.070
An automaton?

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.230
Mikhail?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.400
Did the letter truly bear that name?

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.530
He's alive?

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.240
This is bad.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.250
Stay away from him!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.040
He is...

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.430
We didn't even introduce ourselves.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.050
You're quite hasty, aren't you?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.730
A cover of blue leather,
pages as black as night,

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.810
a clockwork grimoire
linked to a silver chain...

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:21.440
Let's try that again. I am Mikhail.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.070
Only this book was passed down to me
by the Vampire of the Blue Moon.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.740
Yet I'm but a human!

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.960
There is another <i>Book of Vanitas</i>?

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:44.510
Just kidding. I was
channeling my big brother!

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:48.390
Of course, you know who
that is, right, Monsieur Noé?

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:53.770
My big brother is the
one you all call Vanitas.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:58.100
You told Mademoiselle Domi
what my brother said to you.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:02.190
And then Mademoiselle Domi told me.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:05.780
But all these monsieurs and
mademoiselles are getting tedious.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.660
Shall we drop them?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:11.370
Hasn't my big brother
told you anything about me?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.910
You know, like, "I have
a darling little brother."

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.830
Or did he mention Number 71?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.170
How is Number 71 doing?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.500
You're 71?!

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:25.590
I came here today to ask you a favor, Noé.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.220
Domi!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:37.730
She won't hesitate to jump
if anyone lays a finger on me.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.230
Why's he doing this?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.110
You don't want that, do you?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.310
I don't, either.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.190
Don't tell me...

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:48.780
Mademoiselle Domi is so kind. I'd hate
to see her splatter on the ground.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.070
Did he do something to her true name?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:55.330
So, I want you to suck my brother's blood.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.500
What?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.670
There's something I simply must know.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:05.210
I need to know why my
brother killed Father that day.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:09.930
But he never will tell me when I ask.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:16.020
So I'd like you to take a peek for me.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:20.310
You're good at that
sort of thing, aren't you?

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:26.650
Sink your fangs into his pale skin, Noé.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.820
Lay bare that memory in Vanitas's blood.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.990
Dominique's missing?!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:36.540
Indeed she is. She failed
to report for duty at the castle.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.370
A messenger was sent to
Marquis de Sade's manor,

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:44.130
but it's been three days since anyone saw
her at the main residence or the villa.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:50.510
Being that she is of House de Sade,
we cannot rule out capricious action.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.760
Dominique would never do such a thing!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:57.560
She has never once
neglected her royal guard duty.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.770
Three days ago? That's when we last met.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.770
Did something happen after that?

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.940
Jeanne.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.480
May I ask you a favor?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.160
I don't understand.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:22.330
This person you call "Father."

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:27.630
Are you saying Vanitas killed him?

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:31.970
Huh? Wait a moment.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.720
Oh, right...

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.560
Sorry. I was a bit startled by that.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.770
It seems I jumped to conclusions.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.520
After all this time together...

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:52.400
...you don't know a thing
about my brother, do you, Noé?

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.320
Now I see.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:17:00.080
Telling you to suck my brother's
blood has thrown you for a loop.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.120
I know!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:19.930
Instead of his blood,
help yourself to mine.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:27.940
First, I'll use my blood to
tell you all about my brother.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.020
Well, come on.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.940
I'll catch cold if you don't hurry.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:37.160
And mademoiselle will, too.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.240
Domi.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.370
Domi. What happened to your hair?

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.250
Why would you...?

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.920
This? I cut it off
because it was in the way.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.920
Does it suit me, Noé?

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:09.770
I must do all I can to protect Domi.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.770
Even if...

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.320
...it costs me my life.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.570
It's time, Noé.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.730
She, or should I say,
he is the child who survived?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.440
Yes, he was found hiding under a bed.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.110
The Church took him into its care.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:55.280
His mother was a prostitute.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.150
Why'd she dress him like a girl?

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:02.910
It seems she was offering
the child to her best customers.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:15.300
You must not go in there.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.970
You'll never find your way out once
you enter the underground level.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.840
It's a scary maze down there.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:25.180
A mummy! It's alive!

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.310
Huh?

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.480
I'm going to eat you!

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.110
Monsieur?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.280
Yes?

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:40.030
When can I go home?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:45.120
You have a new home starting from today.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:49.410
I hear that there are lots
of children your age there.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:52.040
I'm sure you'll make new friends.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.750
I don't understand.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.750
You'll see.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.760
Monsieur?

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.260
Yes?

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:05.220
Why did they have to kill that vampire?

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:10.180
That vampire killed your mother.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:14.480
No, he saved her!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:20.820
My mother made a really
scary face when she would hit me.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.200
But I knew better.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:28.950
She only did that when the
demon inside her was being bad.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.710
She was also mad

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:35.040
the whole time the vampire was there.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:40.460
But after that, her kind
face slowly returned.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:44.590
My mother was really pretty!

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:51.520
I bet that vampire got rid
of the demon inside her!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.230
Dear God...

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.480
What's wrong, monsieur?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.730
You poor child.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:02.860
The vampires have already led you astray.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:08.330
O Lord, I beseech you!
Please forgive this child!

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.660
O Lord!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.500
Roland!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:15.000
I told you!
You must rest until you're well!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.250
--Wait! I'm helping this child!
--Don't sneak out of your room!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:28.010
Yes, but the child you procured for me
last time broke almost immediately.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.270
And just when I was
hoping for a replacement,

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.850
I found this one in
the most convenient place!

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:38.110
There's no need to worry!

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:41.980
They're scrambling to deal
with that prostitute's murder.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.530
If a child in their care goes missing,

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:48.240
they'll chalk it up to a runaway
and leave it at that.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.160
The child's awakened!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:54.330
All right, I'll have you
look after this one!

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:58.460
I'm counting on you,

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.710
Number 69!

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.050
"Scars"

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:41.540
"Blue Night"
